  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Turn and save",
  "description": "Place three piles of balls just outside the penalty area: one on the left, one straight in front of the goal and one on the right. The goalkeeper stands in the goal with their back to the ice, facing into the goal.\n\nThe coach stands by one of the piles and calls out. The goalkeeper turns round, finds the ball, gets into position and the coach shoots straight away. Between shots the coach moves quietly between the piles so the goalkeeper never knows where the next shot is coming from. Do 8–10 shots, rest and go again.\n\nProgressions: less time between the call and the shot, or mix shots along the ice with lofted balls. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turn quickly and find the ball with your eyes before you move."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Get into position between the ball and the middle of the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Be balanced with your weight on both skates when the shot comes."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
